<title>GERMANY: Valora, Springer take over Stilke.</title>
<headline>Valora, Springer take over Stilke.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's Valora Holding AG and German publisher Axel Springer Verlag AG have taken over Stilke GmbH from a unit of Douglas Holding AG, Springer and Douglas said on Monday in separate statements.</p>
<p>Valora will take a 76 percent stake in the bookstore chain -- which has 70 branches in north German railway stations and at Hamburg airport -- while Springer will buy the remaining 24 percent. The takeover takes effect on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Stilke has annual turnover of 150 million marks and 430 staff, and will continue to be headed by chief executive Peter Juergen Carstensen.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
